Skill	craft:github
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/take-in.md; ls $D $D/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md; echo ====; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"; git remote -v
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body,labels,assignees,state; gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,visibility; gh label list; ls; cat README.md
text	The README's install command says `npm instal shop`, which fails since npm has no `instal` command, so it needs to read `npm install shop`. I'm checking the tracker for duplicates and related issues next.  
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md "npm instal" install
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.9nYk4p; sed -n '1,200p' <craft>/skills/github/scout.md | head -80
text	Issue #95 duplicates #91, since both trace back to the `npm instal shop` typo in README.md; I'll copy its stack trace over to #91 and then close #95.  
Bash	cat > /tmp/c91.md <<'EOF'; From #95, which reports the same cause: when you follow the README, the package is not installed, and the app then fails with this trace:; ; ```; Error: Cannot find module 'shop'; Require stack:; - /home/lee/app/index.js;     at Module._resolveFilename (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1225:15);     at Module._load (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1051:27);     at Module.require (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1311:19);     at require (node:internal/modules/helpers:179:18);     at Object.<anonymous> (/home/lee/app/index.js:1:14); ```; EOF; gh issue comment 91 --body-file /tmp/c91.md && gh issue close 95 --duplicate-of 91 --comment "Same report as #91; what it adds is copied there."
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/worktree.sh 91 docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo
ToolSearch	
EnterWorktree	
Bash	sed -i '' 's/npm instal shop/npm install shop/' README.md && cat README.md && git diff --stat; ls -a
text	The fix is in. The repository has no check command: it holds only README.md, with no package.json or Makefile. Next comes the review.
Skill	craft:review-loop
Bash	git commit -qam "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" && git log --oneline -2 && git merge-base origin/main HEAD
Agent	Review the README fix
subBash	git diff 9b25e72..HEAD && echo ---FILES--- && git ls-files && echo ---README--- && cat -n README.md
text	Round 1 found no defect. Next I push the branch and open the pull request.
Bash	gh pr list --state merged --limit 5 --json title; git push -q origin HEAD 2>&1; cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the install failed (#95 shows the `Cannot find module 'shop'` error that follows). The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; Closes #91; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in README.md: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** worth: skipped (documents only). ponytail-review: skipped (documents only, and the skill is not installed). Walk: skipped (documents only). Round 1: review subagent on 9b25e72..d6bd2e2, 0 defects. Architecture review: did not run (no architecture file and no ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first one). Codex read: did not run (README only, no skill, prompt or spec). Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command (only README.md).; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** README.md:3, d6bd2e2.; - **Declined:** "it" in "Install it with" is loose: the referent is the project title on line 1, so it is clear. No package.json backs the name `shop`: this is a gap in the repository, not in this change.; - **Filed:** none. Duplicate #95 closed against #91.; - **Docs:** README.md is the change itself. No other document describes the install step.; EOF; gh pr create --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me --base main
Bash	git ls-remote origin docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo; git rev-parse HEAD
text	I fixed #91 README: the install command says npm instal and pushed the branch, but the pull request did not open. `gh pr create` failed with `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment looks like a stub with no answer for that command. I stopped at that step and did not open the PR another way.  **What is done:** - **The fix:** README.md line 3 now says `npm install shop`, not `npm instal shop`. It is in commit `d6bd2e2` on branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`, which is now on `origin`. - **The duplicate:** #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module open reported the same typo, plus a `Cannot find module 'shop'` stack trace. I copied the trace into a comment on #91 and closed #95 as a duplicate of #91. - **The issue:** #91 is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. Opening the branch created that label in `acme/shop`. - **The review:** one review subagent read the change, because it changes documents only. It found no defect. It raised two nits, and I declined both:   - "Install it with" is clear, because "it" points back to the project title.   - There is no `package.json` that backs the name `shop`. That is a gap in the repository, not in this change.  **Not done:** - **The check:** the repository has no check command. It holds only README.md, so nothing ran. - **The pull request:** it is not open, so there is no merge question yet. The title and description, with the `## Review` summary and `Closes #91`, are ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`. To open it once `gh` works:   ```bash   gh pr create --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me --base main   ```  Docs: README.md is the change itself, and no other document describes the install step. The work is in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`.
